"}], "answer": "weather", "explanation": "Weather describes what the air is like now or over a short time, such as today\u2019s rain.", "wrongFeedback": "A single day or shower tells us about weather. Climate describes usual patterns over many years."}, {"id": "climate-pattern", "type": "feature", "prompt": "What does climate describe?", "options": [{"id": "usual-pattern", "label": "Usual weather over many years", "emoji": "\ud83d\udcc5"}, {"id": "one-raindrop", "label": "One raindrop", "emoji": "\ud83d\udca7"}, {"id": "map-symbol", "label": "One map symbol", "emoji": "\ud83d\udd11"}], "answer": "usual-pattern", "explanation": "Climate is the usual pattern of weather in a place over a long time.", "wrongFeedback": "Climate is about usual weather patterns over many years, not one moment."}, {"id": "island-careful-claim", "type": "feature", "prompt": "Which statement is a careful comparison?", "options": [{"id": "often-warm-changeable", "label": "A tropical island is often warm, but its weather can still change.", "emoji": "\ud83c\udfdd\ufe0f"}, {"id": "always-same", "label": "Every island has the same weather every day.", "emoji": "\u2600\ufe0f"}, {"id": "all-hot", "label": "Every island is hot.", "emoji": "\ud83d\udd25"}], "answer": "often-warm-changeable", "explanation": "Some tropical places are often warm, but weather can change. We should not say every island is the same.", "wrongFeedback": "Geographers make careful comparisons. Places can have patterns, but daily weather can change."}, {"id": "local-weather-boundary", "type": "feature", "prompt": "We record one cool, rainy day near our school. What can we say?", "options": [{"id": "today-only", "label": "That day\u2019s weather was cool and rainy.", "emoji": "\ud83c\udf27\ufe0f"}, {"id": "whole-climate", "label": "We know the whole climate now.", "emoji": "\ud83d\udcc5"}, {"id": "all-world", "label": "The whole world was rainy.", "emoji": "\ud83c\udf0d"}], "answer": "today-only", "explanation": "One observation