\ud83c\udf0d"}, {"id": "future-events", "label": "Future events", "emoji": "\ud83d\udd2e"}], "answer": "their-memory", "explanation": "An interview can share one person\u2019s memory. Historians compare it with photographs and other clues before making a wider claim.", "wrongFeedback": "One interview tells us about that person\u2019s memory, not everyone\u2019s experience."}, {"id": "history-compare-sources", "type": "evidence", "prompt": "An old photo shows a small playground. A former pupil remembers a larger one. What should a time detective do?", "options": [{"id": "check-more", "label": "Compare more sources", "emoji": "\ud83d\udd0e"}, {"id": "choose-favourite", "label": "Pick the favourite answer", "emoji": "\ud83c\udfb2"}, {"id": "ignore-both", "label": "Ignore both clues", "emoji": "\ud83d\ude48"}], "answer": "check-more", "explanation": "Sources can show different details. Check dates, ask another question and compare another photograph or plan.", "wrongFeedback": "When clues differ, compare more evidence and check when each source was made."}, {"id": "history-photo-limit", "type": "evidence", "prompt": "An old photograph shows a shop front. Which conclusion is safest?", "options": [{"id": "looks-like", "label": "We can describe how it looked.", "emoji": "\ud83c\udfea"}, {"id": "knows-thoughts", "label": "We know every shopper\u2019s thoughts.", "emoji": "\ud83d\udcad"}, {"id": "knows-all-history", "label": "We know everything about the shop.", "emoji": "\ud83d\udcda"}], "answer": "looks-like", "explanation": "A photograph is useful for visible details, but it does not tell us everything about people or events.", "wrongFeedback": "A photograph can show visible details. It cannot show every thought or tell the whole story."}, {"id": "history-local-change", "type": "evidence", "prompt": "Which pair gives two different kinds of clues about how a local street changed?", "options": [{"id": "old-photo-new-map", "label": "An old photo and a modern map", "emoji": "\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f"}, {"id": "two-guesses", "label": "Two guesses", "emoji": "\ud83c\udfb2"}, {"id": "future-story", "label": "A story about tomorrow", "emoji": "\ud83d\udd2e"}], "answer": "old-photo-new-map", "explanation": "An old photo can show what the street looked like, while a modern map can show today\u2019s layout. Comparing them helps us notice change.", "wrongFeedback": "Choose sources connected to the street and made at different times."}, {"id": "history-photos", "type": "evidence", "prompt": "A time detective wants to learn what an old seaside holiday looked like. Which clue is most useful?", "options": [{"id": "old-photo", "label": "An old photograph", "emoji": "\ud83d\udcf7"}, {"id": "new-toy", "label": "A toy bought yesterday", "emoji": "\ud83e\uddf8"}, {"id": "guess", "label": "A wild guess", "emoji": "\ud83d\udcad"}], "answer": "old-photo", "explanation": "An old photograph can show visible details, but it cannot tell us everything people thought or felt.", "wrongFeedback": "Choose a clue made at the time. A source can help, but every source has limits."}, {"id": "history-castle", "type": "evidence", "prompt": "Which source could help us investigate a castle long ago?", "options": [{"id": "castle-artefact", "label": "An artefact found there", "emoji": "\ud83c\udffa"}, {"id": "weather-app", "label": "Today\u2019s weather app", "emoji": "\ud83d\udcf1"}, {"id": "future-map", "label": "A map of a future city", "emoji": "\ud83d\udef8"}], "answer": "castle-artefact", "explanation": "An artefact is one object from the past. Historians compare it with other sources.", "wrongFeedback": "Look for something connected to the castle in the past. Historians compare more than one clue."}, {"id": "history-communication", "type": "sequence", "prompt": "Put these ways to send a message from oldest to newest.", "items": [{"id": "letter", "label": "Handwritten letter", "emoji": "\u2709\ufe0f", "order": 1}, {"id": "telephone", "label": "Landline telephone", "emoji": "