i": "\ud83e\uddcd"}], "answer": "wood", "explanation": "A chair is an object. Wood is the material it can be made from.", "wrongFeedback": "The object is the chair. The material is wood."}, {"id": "science-material-waterproof", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which material is usually useful for keeping rain out of a raincoat?", "options": [{"id": "plastic", "label": "Plastic", "emoji": "\ud83e\udde5"}, {"id": "paper", "label": "Paper", "emoji": "\ud83d\udcc4"}, {"id": "sponge", "label": "Sponge", "emoji": "\ud83e\uddfd"}], "answer": "plastic", "explanation": "Plastic can be waterproof, so it can help keep rain out. The exact material and design still matter.", "wrongFeedback": "A raincoat needs a material that keeps water out. Plastic can be waterproof."}, {"id": "science-material-absorbent", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which material is usually absorbent for wiping up a small spill?", "options": [{"id": "paper", "label": "Paper", "emoji": "\ud83d\udcc4"}, {"id": "glass", "label": "Glass", "emoji": "\ud83e\ude9f"}, {"id": "metal", "label": "Metal", "emoji": "\ud83e\udd44"}], "answer": "paper", "explanation": "Paper can absorb water. Glass and metal are usually not absorbent.", "wrongFeedback": "Absorbent materials soak up liquid. Paper is the best choice here."}, {"id": "science-material-shape", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which action can change the shape of a soft piece of clay?", "options": [{"id": "squash", "label": "Squash it", "emoji": "\ud83d\udc50"}, {"id": "listen", "label": "Listen to it", "emoji": "\ud83d\udc42"}, {"id": "count", "label": "Count it", "emoji": "\ud83d\udd22"}], "answer": "squash", "explanation": "Squashing, bending, twisting or stretching can change the shape of some materials.", "wrongFeedback": "Some materials change shape when we squash, bend, twist or stretch them."}, {"id": "science-material-group", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which two objects could be grouped because they are made from metal?", "options": [{"id": "spoon-key", "label": "Spoon and key", "emoji": "\ud83e\udd44\ud83d\udd11"}, {"id": "balloon-shirt", "label": "Balloon and shirt", "emoji": "\ud83c\udf88\ud83d\udc55"}, {"id": "book-window", "label": "Book and window", "emoji": "\ud83d\udcd6\ud83e\ude9f"}], "answer": "spoon-key", "explanation": "A spoon and a key can both be made from metal. We group objects by a property or material.", "wrongFeedback": "Group objects using their material. A spoon and key can both be metal."}, {"id": "science-season-record", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which record could help us compare weather each day?", "options": [{"id": "weather-chart", "label": "A weather chart", "emoji": "\ud83d\udcca"}, {"id": "single-guess", "label": "One guess", "emoji": "\ud83c\udfb2"}, {"id": "story-only", "label": "A story with no dates", "emoji": "\ud83d\udcd6"}], "answer": "weather-chart", "explanation": "A dated weather chart lets us compare observations across days.", "wrongFeedback": "To compare weather, record observations with dates in a chart or table."}, {"id": "science-season-spring", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which change might we observe as spring begins?", "options": [{"id": "buds-open", "label": "Buds opening", "emoji": "\ud83c\udf31"}, {"id": "always-snow", "label": "Snow every day", "emoji": "\u2744\ufe0f"}, {"id": "no-daylight", "label": "No daylight", "emoji": "\ud83c\udf11"}], "answer": "buds-open", "explanation": "Plants may grow new leaves or flowers in spring. Weather varies, so this is an observation to check, not a promise for every day.", "wrongFeedback": "Buds opening can be a spring change. Keep seasonal statements as observations, because weather varies."}, {"id": "science-enquiry-question", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which is a question a scientist could investigate?", "options": [{"id": "paper-absorb", "label": "Which paper absorbs more water?", "emoji": "\ud83d\udca7"}, {"id": "best-ever", "label": "What is the best thing ever?", "emoji": "\ud83c\udfc6"}, {"id": "magic-answer", "label": "Can magic answer it?", "emoji": "\u2728"}], "answer": "paper-absorb", "explanation": "A simple question can be tested by observing and recording what happens.", "wrongFeedback": "Choose a question that can be explored with an observation or simple test."}, {"id": "science-fair-test", "type": "classify", "prompt": "To compare two paper towels fairly, what should we try to keep the same?", "options": [{"id": "same-water", "label": "The amount of water", "emoji": "\ud83d\udca7"}, {"id": "different-everything", "label": "Everything different", "emoji": "\ud83c\udfb2"}, {"id": "no-record", "label": "No record", "emoji": "\ud83d\ude48"}], "answer": "same-water", "explanation": "Keeping the amount of water the same makes the comparison fairer. We can change one thing and observe the result.", "wrongFeedback": "Keep important conditions the same so the comparison is fair."}, {"id": "science-observe-tool", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which tool can help us observe a small leaf closely?", "options": [{"id": "hand-lens", "label": "Hand lens", "emoji": "\ud83d\udd0e"}, {"id": "pillow", "label": "Pillow", "emoji": "\ud83d\udecf\ufe0f"}, {"id": "whistle", "label": "Whistle", "emoji": "\ud83d\udcef"}], "answer": "hand-lens", "explanation": "A hand lens magnifies small details so we can observe closely.", "wrongFeedback": "A hand lens helps us see small details."}, {"id": "science-record-data", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which way could we record how many red and green leaves we found?", "options": [{"id": "tally-table", "label": "A tally table", "emoji": "\ud83d\udccb"}, {"id": "secret-guess", "label": "A secret guess", "emoji": "\ud83e\udd2b"}, {"id": "blank-page", "label": "A blank page", "emoji": "\ud83d\udcc4"}], "answer": "tally-table", "explanation": "A tally table helps us count and compare groups of observations.", "wrongFeedback": "Use a table or tally to record and compare observations."}, {"id": "science-plant", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which one is a plant?", "options": [{"id": "oak", "label": "Oak tree", "emoji": "\ud83c\udf33"}, {"id": "fox", "label": "Fox", "emoji": "\ud83e\udd8a"}, {"id": "rock", "label": "Rock", "emoji": "\ud83e\udea8"}], "answer": "oak", "explanation": "An oak tree is a plant. It grows and needs light and water.", "wrongFeedback": "A plant grows. A fox is an animal and a rock is not living."}, {"id": "science-animal", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which one is an animal?", "options": [{"id": "frog", "label": "Frog", "emoji": "\ud83d\udc38"}, {"id": "fern", "label": "Fern", "emoji": "\ud83c\udf3f"}, {"id": "glass", "label": "Glass", "emoji": "\ud83e\udd5b"}], "answer": "frog", "explanation": "A frog is an animal. Animals move, feed and grow.", "wrongFeedback": "A fern is a plant and glass is a material. A frog is the animal."}, {"id": "science-material", "type": "classify", "prompt": "A window must be see-through. Which material is useful?", "options": [{"id": "clear-glass", "label": "Clear glass", "emoji": "\ud83e\ude9f"}, {"id": "wool", "label": "Wool", "emoji": "\ud83e\uddf6"}, {"id": "brick", "label": "Brick", "emoji": "\ud83e\uddf1"}], "answer": "clear-glass", "explanation": "Clear glass is transparent, so we can see through it. The window is the object; glass is its material.", "wrongFeedback": "Think about the property the object needs. A window needs a transparent material."}, {"id": "science-season", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which season often has the warmest days?", "options": [{"id": "summer", "label": "Summer", "emoji": "\u2600\ufe0f"}, {"id": "winter", "label": "Winter", "emoji": "\u2744\ufe0f"}, {"id": "autumn", "label": "Autumn", "emoji": "\ud83c\udf42"}], "answer": "summer", "explanation": "Summer often has the warmest days, although weather can change.", "wrongFeedback": "Winter is usually colder. Summer often has the warmest days."}, {"id": "science-plant-needs", "type": "classify", "prompt": "What does a green plant need to grow?", "options": [{"id": "